The Importance of Digital Literacy in the Modern World
Digital literacy is no longer optional; it is a fundamental life skill. It goes beyond knowing how to open a browser or send a message.
It includes the ability to find, evaluate, and critically use information from digital sources. A digitally literate person can distinguish reliable news from misinformation,
protect their personal data, and navigate online services safely. 
Learning these skills empowers individuals to participate fully in education, employment, and civic life, and it reduces the risk of being manipulated or exploited online.
